{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q5277238","formula":"C₁₃H₁₇NO₂","hill":"C13H17NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":17.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"2-(5-methoxy-1-benzofuran-3-yl)-N,N-dimethylethanamine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Dimemebfe, also known as 5-methoxy-N,N-dimethyl-3-(2-aminoethyl)benzofuran (5-MeO-BFE or 5-MeO-DMBF) or as 1-oxa-5-MeO-DMT, is a psychedelic drug of the benzofuran family related to the psychedelic tryptamine 5-MeO-DMT. It is the analogue and bioisostere of 5-MeO-DMT in which the nitrogen atom of the indole ring has been replaced with an oxygen atom, making dimemebfe a benzofuran rather than tryptamine derivative. The drug has been encountered as a novel designer drug."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":126589,"mass":219.28,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN(C)CCC1=COC2=C1C=C(C=C2)OC","inchikey":"WBPQJTBOQCCTFX-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(5-methoxy-1-benzofuran-3-yl)-N,N-dimethylethanamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"126589","atoms":33,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.699,"y":2.722,"z":0.143,"el":"O"},{"x":2.883,"y":-2.276,"z":-0.102,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.083,"y":-0.678,"z":0.04,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.032,"y":0.44,"z":-0.774,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.77,"y":1.108,"z":-0.406,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.858,"y":-0.037,"z":0.437,"el":"C"},{"x":0.5,"y":0.501,"z":-0.219,"el":"C"},{"x":1.368,"y":1.535,"z":0.117,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.594,"y":2.453,"z":-0.175,"el":"C"},{"x":1.011,"y":-0.807,"z":-0.296,"el":"C"},{"x":2.724,"y":1.36,"z":0.385,"el":"C"},{"x":2.372,"y":-1.014,"z":-0.032,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.88,"y":-1.079,"z":1.21,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.823,"y":-1.854,"z":-0.804,"el":"C"},{"x":3.211,"y":0.052,"z":0.302,"el":"C"},{"x":4.273,"y":-2.427,"z":0.176,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.773,"y":-0.398,"z":-1.43,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.642,"y":1.123,"z":-1.38,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.241,"y":